23 open findings: 9 MustChange/rewrite, 10 rewrite_recommended, 4 NiceToRewrite_ifTimePermits (priorities: 3 Blocker, 12 Major, 8 Minor). Prefix CCN-FR-.
Headline	Why it matters
CCN-FR-1 OperacionServicio and CalypsoMqServicio take the concrete ConfiguracionServicio, but only Configuracion is registered	with SimpleInjector 5.x the Verify() at ServiceHost.cs:87 fails and the service cannot start (reproduced); with 4.x each consumer silently gets its own blank configuration, so the MQ URI read by one class is null in the other
CCN-FR-2 the request is published to MQ first and marked SENT afterwards, in separate non-atomic steps	if the marking fails (or the process stops between the two calls) the same FX trade message is published again on every following tick until someone fixes the row
CCN-FR-3 responses are consumed with AutoAcknowledge, then written to SQL one by one; the first failure abandons the rest of the batch	acknowledgements from Calypso (and liquidation messages) are lost for good; the request stays SENT forever and nothing alerts
CCN-FR-4 / 5 CalypsoId is never extracted (always empty) and usp_RegistrarRespuestaCalypso_Conector is not idempotent	the Calypso trade id never reaches tbl_calypso_intercambio; a duplicated or malformed message inserts extra RECV rows that Calypso_Liquidacion treats as settlement instructions
CCN-FR-6 / 7 MQ/DB failures are log-only (the alerting catch is unreachable) and configuration errors skip the termination marker	an ActiveMQ outage looks like a quiet day; the TOMI execution row stays "running"
CCN-FR-8 four of the five unit tests depend on the wall clock and none touch the infrastructure, SQL or DI	the tests cannot catch FR-1 to FR-5 and fail when run before 06:10

Business context: Calypso_Conector is the MQ bridge between the TOMI exchange table tbl_calypso_intercambio and the Calypso treasury system. A defect here either books an FX trade twice, loses its confirmation, or loses a liquidation instruction, so the hand-off defects (FR-2, FR-3, FR-5) take priority over everything else.
