CCN-FR-2 (Blocker) - "publish, then mark `SENT`" is not atomic: a failed or interrupted mark re-publishes the same FX trade on every tick. OperacionServicio.cs:238-265 and the procedures behind it:
Code block (csharp)
var solicitudes = await _iCalypsoIntercambio.ObtenerSolicitudesPendientesAsync(tipo);            // :244  rows with estatus = 'INI'
foreach (CalypsoIntercambioMensaje solicitud in solicitudes)                                      // :250
{
    _iCalypsoMqServicio.InsertarMensaje(_configuracion.StrCalypsoMQReq, mensaje);                 // :257  message is on the broker
    await _iCalypsoIntercambio.MarcarSolicitudEnviadaAsync(solicitud.IdEnvio);                    // :258  separate DB transaction
}
// catch (Exception ex) { log }                                                                   // :261  rest of the batch abandoned
The two operations cannot be made atomic across ActiveMQ and SQL Server, so the order decides the failure mode. Here the broker write comes first: if MarcarSolicitudEnviadaAsync throws (SQL timeout, deadlock, the Exito=false branch at CalypsoIntercambio.cs:72-75) or the service is stopped between the two calls, the row is still INI, the next tick (10 s later) selects it again (usp_ObtenerSolicitudesPendientesCalypso_Conector.sql:39) and publishes the same message again - for as long as the update keeps failing. The catch at :261 also abandons the remaining rows of the batch. Nothing correlates the request to the response on the broker side (InsertarMensaje sets no correlation id or message id, CalypsoMqServicio.cs:86-88), so Calypso cannot de-duplicate by transport metadata either; whether it de-duplicates by ExternalRef is unknown. usp_MarcarSolicitudEnviadaCalypso_Conector.sql:45-47 also updates by id_envio only - no estatus = 'INI' guard and no @@ROWCOUNT check - so a vanished row reports success. Fix: claim before publishing, publish, then confirm; never re-publish a claimed row without a human decision.
Code block (sql)
-- 1) claim a bounded batch, oldest first (INI -> SNDNG); only the claimer sees the rows
;WITH c AS (SELECT TOP (@max) * FROM dbo.tbl_calypso_intercambio WITH (UPDLOCK, READPAST, ROWLOCK)
            WHERE estatus = 'INI' AND tipo = @tipo ORDER BY id_envio)
UPDATE c SET estatus = 'SNDNG' OUTPUT inserted.id_envio AS IdEnvio, inserted.msg_in AS MensajeEntrada, inserted.external_ref AS ExternalRef;
-- 2) usp_Marcar...: UPDATE ... SET estatus='SENT' WHERE id_envio=@id AND estatus='SNDNG'; IF @@ROWCOUNT <> 1 THROW 50001, 'Fila no reservada', 1;
Code block (csharp)
foreach (var s in await _iCalypsoIntercambio.ReservarSolicitudesAsync(tipo, maxLote))        // INI -> SNDNG
{
    try { _iCalypsoMqServicio.InsertarMensaje(cola, s.MensajeEntrada, correlationId: s.ExternalRef); }
    catch { await _iCalypsoIntercambio.LiberarSolicitudAsync(s.IdEnvio); throw; }               // nothing published: back to INI
    await _iCalypsoIntercambio.MarcarSolicitudEnviadaAsync(s.IdEnvio);                          // published: if this fails the row stays SNDNG, alert, do NOT re-send
}
Add a runbook line for rows stuck in SNDNG (published but unconfirmed) and make the FX publisher set the message NMSCorrelationID to ExternalRef. Benefit: a database fault can no longer multiply trade submissions; the failure mode becomes "one trade needs manual confirmation", which is visible. Suggested JIRA: CCN-2 (Blocker). Related: FCM-FR-6 in FCMConector (same hand-off, GEN-18).
