EjecutaProcedimientosAsync wraps RealizaOperacionesAsync in a try whose catch raises a Critical alert (:179-196), but RealizaOperacionesAsync and both helpers catch everything themselves, so that catch can only fire for failures in the lines it does not contain - in practice never. When ActiveMQ is down (Conectar throws) or usp_RegistrarRespuestaCalypso_Conector fails, the tick ends "successfully", the only trace is a log line, and the message "Validar manualmente" tells no one. The unit test CuandoMQFalla_NoRevientaYMArxaFinalizacion even asserts this behaviour without checking for an alert. Separately, EmviaAlerta discards the Task returned by InsertarAlerta (_ =): a failed insert is unobserved and the alert may still be in flight when the tick (or the service) ends - the only escalation channel is itself lossy. Fix: let the three methods collect failures and rethrow (or return a typed result) so the single outer catch raises one alert per failed tick; make the alert awaited and its result checked.
