CCN-FR-10 (Major) - out-of-hours and non-business-day ticks log ERROR/raise a Critical alert on every tick (GEN-10); the window comparison is brittle. OperacionServicio.cs:122-165 and :169-177:
Code block (csharp)
if (StrFechaSistema >= StrHoraOperacionesInicio && StrFechaSistema <= StrHoraOperacionesFin) ...   // :124-125  TimeSpan with seconds
alertaSistema.ClaveAviso = ConstantesClaveAviso.Critico; ... EmviaAlerta(alertaSistema);             // :153-161  every out-of-hours tick
Config.EscribirLog($"ERROR|Ejecuta_Procedimientos|Hoy es un día inhábil.", ...);                     // :176  ERROR every holiday tick
Outside the window the service raises a Critical alert row per tick (about 360 rows per hour at the 10 s fallback interval; usp_InsertaAlerta_MUFGLibreria does not de-duplicate - GEN-10), and every holiday tick logs an ERROR. The test StrFechaSistema <= Fin compares the full time of day with seconds: with a 23:59 end (the value used in the tests), 23:59:01 is already "outside" and the service starts raising Critical alerts one minute before midnight. There is no support for an overnight window (inicio > fin never matches) and the ParseTimeSpanRequerido helper accepts "8" as eight days (related GEN-12 note SOCS-FR-4). Fix: model the window as a state (Dentro/Fuera/Inhabil), log only transitions at INFO, alert at most once per transition, compare minutes, support overnight windows:
Code block (csharp)
var ahora = new TimeSpan(hora.Hours, hora.Minutes, 0);
bool dentro = inicio <= fin ? ahora >= inicio && ahora <= fin : ahora >= inicio || ahora <= fin;
Benefit: no alert storm, no false alarms at the window edge. Suggested JIRA: CCN-10 (Major). Standing finding: GEN-10.
CCN-FR-16 (Minor) - duplicated blocks: two alert builders, an 8-case parameter switch, and an undisposed `Process` per alert. OperacionServicio.cs:149-161 and :183-194 build an AlertaDTO field by field (same five assignments, only Exception differs); both call Process.GetCurrentProcess() twice (:149-150, :183-184) although _configuracion.Pid/NombreProceso are already loaded by the shared startup, and Process is IDisposable (two handles per alert, left to the finalizer). The switch at :64-107 has eight cases that each assign one property and (for six of them) write one log line whose wording alone differs; the mapping is data, not logic. Fix: one private AlertaDTO CrearAlerta(Exception ex) using _configuracion.Pid ?? 0/NombreProceso, and a Dictionary<ParametrosSistema, Action<ConfiguracionServicio, string>> (or a validated ParametrosCalypso DTO, see FR-7). Benefit: about 70 lines become about 25; the same helper serves FR-6 and FR-10. Suggested JIRA: CCN-16 (Minor).
CCN-FR-18 (Minor) - cancellation is ignored: `ct` is never used inside the tick. EjecutaProcedimientosAsync(CancellationToken ct) (:45) never reads ct; the MQ drain (up to 2 x 10 x 1 s receive timeouts) and the SQL calls cannot be interrupted, so a service stop waits for the whole tick, and an OperationCanceledException thrown by the shared calls would be reported as a Critical alert by the generic catch (:179-196). Fix: pass ct to the repositories, add catch (OperationCanceledException) { throw; } before the generic catch and finalise with CancellationToken.None. Benefit: clean stop, no spurious critical alert. Suggested JIRA: CCN-18 (Minor). Related: FCM-FR-19.
