CCN-FR-3 (Blocker) - responses are acknowledged on receipt (`AutoAcknowledge`), registered afterwards one by one, and the first failure abandons the rest: acknowledgements and liquidation messages can be lost permanently. CalypsoMqServicio.cs:44, :118-170 and OperacionServicio.cs:273-289:
Code block (csharp)
_session = _connection.CreateSession(AcknowledgementMode.AutoAcknowledge);                    // :44  broker deletes the message when Receive returns
IMessage mensajeMq = consumidor.Receive(new TimeSpan(0, 0, 0, 0, 1000));                       // :120
if (textoMq == null) { Config.EscribirLog($"AVISO|..."); continue; }                           // :128-135  non-text message: consumed and dropped
...  mensajes.Add(respuesta);                                                                   // up to 10 messages held only in memory
// OperacionServicio.cs
var mensajes = _iCalypsoMqServicio.LeerMensajes(idQueue);                                       // :277  all consumed already
foreach (var mensaje in mensajes) await _iCalypsoIntercambio.RegistrarRespuestaAsync(mensaje, tipo);   // :278-281  throws -> loop aborted -> catch logs "Validar manualmente"
With auto-acknowledge the broker removes each message as soon as Receive returns, but it is written to SQL only later, and LeerMensajes first drains up to ten messages into a list. If RegistrarRespuestaAsync throws for message 3 (SQL timeout, deadlock, Exito=false, a bad value), messages 3 to 10 are already gone from the broker and never written; the matching requests stay SENT forever, no alert is raised (FR-6), and the only trace is the log line. A service stop or crash after the receive has the same effect. Non-text messages are removed and dropped with a warning. Fix: acknowledge only after the database commit, one message at a time, and send failures to a poison path.
Code block (csharp)
_session = _connection.CreateSession(AcknowledgementMode.IndividualAcknowledge);               // Apache.NMS: ack per message
// ICalypsoMqServicio: Task<int> ProcesarMensajesAsync(string cola, Func<CalypsoRespuestaMq, Task> registrar, int max, TimeSpan presupuesto)
var m = consumidor.Receive(espera);
try { await registrar(Convertir(m)); m.Acknowledge(); }                                          // commit first, ack second
